 "notes": {
  "n-status": {
   "x": 1520,
   "y": 0,
   "w": 480,
   "text": "Final Vendor design · awaiting your acceptance\nAll ten owned screens (VE-01 to VE-09 and VE-13) carry the accepted refinement R1 and its five presentation choices. Overview, My experiments and editor steps 1–2 are the R1 screens you approved; Preview and documents, Check and submit, the record and its history, Revise, Edit draft, read-only and refusal states now use the same patterns. Claude Code integration has not started.",
   "fill": "orange"
  },
  "n-play": {
   "x": 2040,
   "y": 0,
   "w": 480,
   "text": "How to review\nThe first board is the working Vendor workspace: press Play and use it as Anil Shetty would — sidebar, lists, records, the four-step form, dialogs, Help. The dashed bar above the page is reviewer-only: jump to a screen, load a scenario, fill sample answers, reset; it also explains handoffs to other roles. Every other board opens one screen or state and stays usable; each keeps its own state.",
   "fill": "blue"
  },
  "n-journeys": {
   "x": 2560,
   "y": 0,
   "w": 480,
   "text": "Two demo journeys on the first board\n1 · Create experiment → Save draft with nothing filled → fill → Save draft (SUB-0087) → leave → My experiments → Edit draft → steps 2–4 → Submit → confirm → record → history.\n2 · Overview → Revise “Forced Convection” → read the reason → fix the AR fields → Resubmit → confirm → Submitted · revision 2 in the record, history, list and Overview.",
   "fill": "blue"
  },
  "n-patterns": {
   "x": 3080,
   "y": 0,
   "w": 480,
   "text": "One pattern language across the role\nSections with a title and a six-column field grid · one block per chosen format with a live status · app-package guidance written once · a status pill with one plain line · each page states its status once · sticky actions on long forms · an outline that follows the step · the returned reason with chips that jump to the field · outcome cards with the facts and the next step.",
